  "term": "arbitration",
  "definition": "Arbitration is the voluntary settlement of a dispute by a neutral third person whose authority comes from the parties’ own agreement. It differs from ordinary court proceedings because the submission is by consent, although the parties may also ask the government to enforce the decision.",
